# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hearth environment template. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in.
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
# `.env.local` is gitignored. Never commit real keys.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Supabase project (Project Settings -> API)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your_project_ref.supabase.co/
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_ANON_PUBLIC_KEY

Server-only. Used by privileged server actions and by several signed-in pages
(contractor browse, pro dashboard, parcel lookup). REQUIRED: without it those
pages throw at render time. Never exposed to the browser; bypasses RLS.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

Parcel enrichment (onboarding pre-fill). Optional: when empty the homeowner
types their home facts in by hand. Free key at https://app.rentcast.io/app/api
(50 lookups/month on the free tier) fills year built, sqft, beds/baths, lot
size, and property type from county records.
RENTCAST_API_KEY=

Public site URL (used for auth redirects). Use http://localhost:3000/ locally.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000/

Stripe (Dashboard -> Developers -> API keys / Webhooks). Server-only secrets.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is optional for local development: pages load without it and
only billing actions (checkout, portal, billing outlook) fail, with an error
that names the variable. A test-mode key (sk_test_...) is enough locally.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Recurring price ids for the homeowner "Hearth Plus" plan (Dashboard -> Products).
# All three cadences are sold: weekly, monthly, yearly. Weekly is the one that
# carries the 3-day free trial, so its Price must renew every WEEK. Any of the
# three may be left blank; checkout falls back to inline price_data at the
# amounts in src/lib/constants.ts.
STRIPE_PRICE_PLUS_WEEKLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_PLUS_MONTHLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_PLUS_YEARLY=
# Tiered volume Price ids for the Plus-only pay-per-extra-home add-on (one
# recurring Price each, "volume" tiers matching src/lib/constants.ts EXTRA_HOME).
# Optional: when blank, setExtraHomesAction falls back to inline price_data that
# computes the same volume-discounted unit price, so the add-on works before the
# Prices are created in the Stripe dashboard.
STRIPE_PRICE_HOME_SLOT_MONTHLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_HOME_SLOT_YEARLY=

Anthropic (console.anthropic.com). Powers every AI feature: Ask Hearth,
quote analysis, document and inspection reading, drafts and packets.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

Trial-abuse risk score (migration 0130, src/lib/risk). A long random string used
to salt the one-way hashes of device, network and payment-method identifiers, so
the stored values can never be walked back to an IP address or a card. Generate
with `openssl rand -hex 32`, 16+ characters. NEVER change it after launch: the
hashes are salted with it, so a change makes every previously recorded signal
stop matching and every repeat offender read as brand new. There is NO fallback:
without this variable no signals are recorded at all and every account scores as
clean. Go-live blocker, see docs/GO-LIVE-WIRING.md.
RISK_HASH_SALT=

Whether the risk score is allowed to ACT on what it finds. Defaults to off, and
should stay off for the first week after launch: while it is off the score is
still computed and stored on every checkout, but the free trial is always
granted, so you can read the level distribution out of account_risk and see what
it would have done to real customers before it does it. Set to exactly "true" to
enforce. Even when enforced, nothing refuses a sale - the worst outcome is
"billed from day one instead of day four".
RISK_ENFORCE=false

Cron (Vercel Cron / Supabase scheduled function). Secret the scheduler sends
as the x-cron-secret header (or ?secret=) to authorize /api/cron/alerts.
CRON_SECRET=

Checkr (checkr.com) background checks for pros (0057). Optional: the
background-check UI stays dormant without CHECKR_API_KEY.
CHECKR_API_KEY=
# The Checkr package slug for this account (src/lib/checkr.ts). Leave blank
# to use the "basic_criminal" placeholder - set the real slug before launch.
CHECKR_PACKAGE=

Resend (resend.com/api-keys) - powers the email channel in src/lib/notify.ts.
Optional: email stays dormant without RESEND_API_KEY.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Verified sender, e.g. "Hearth <hello@yourdomain.com>". Leave blank and the
# Resend sandbox sender is used instead, which only delivers to the account
# owner - set this before launch so real recipients get mail.
RESEND_FROM=

Stripe "Hearth Pro" plan (contractor membership, src/app/pro/plus/actions.ts).
Optional: each falls back to a working default (inline price_data / an
auto-created coupon) so checkout works before these are set up in Stripe.
STRIPE_PRO_INTRO_COUPON_ID=
STRIPE_PRO_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID=
STRIPE_PRO_YEARLY_PRICE_ID=

Twilio (twilio.com) - powers the SMS channel in src/lib/notify.ts. Optional:
SMS stays dormant without these, and separately requires per-user
sms_consent (see notify.ts's TCPA gate note).
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=
# TODO(config): must exactly match the "A message comes in" webhook URL
# configured for this number in the Twilio console (scheme + host + path, no
# query string), or genuine Twilio requests fail signature verification.
# Only needed if the forwarded-header fallback in
# src/app/api/twilio/inbound/route.ts proves unreliable for this deployment.
TWILIO_WEBHOOK_URL=

Outbound kill switch (src/lib/outboundGuards.ts, docs/GO-LIVE-WIRING.md section
9). Set to 1 or true to stop every email and SMS at the one send door - the
lever to pull when a cron loops or a preview deploy turns out to be pointed at
the live Resend/Twilio keys. In-app notifications are unaffected. Leave unset.
# OUTBOUND_DISABLED=1

Sign in with Apple (docs/APPLE-SIGN-IN-SETUP.md). The "Continue with Apple"
button is hidden unless this is exactly "1". Leave it blank until the Apple
provider is fully configured in Supabase (step 4 of that doc) - before then
the button can only produce a "provider is not enabled" error, and a dead
button on the sign-in page is worse than no button. Public by necessity: the
check runs in the browser, so this is a visibility flag, not a secret.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APPLE_SIGNIN=

Web Push (src/lib/push.ts, public/sw.js) - the notification that reaches a
phone with the app CLOSED. Costs nothing per message, so it is free for
everyone on both sides. Generate a pair with `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`
and set all three; with any one missing, push is a dormant no-op and the in-app
bell, email and SMS are unaffected. On iPhone this only works once Hearth has
been added to the Home Screen (iOS 16.4+), never in a Safari tab - the UI says
so rather than showing a dead button. See docs/GO-LIVE-WIRING.md section 10.
The public key is deliberately public: the browser needs it to subscribe.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Contact address the push services use if a sender misbehaves. Must be a
# mailto: or https: URL, e.g. mailto:hello@yourdomain.com
VAPID_SUBJECT=

Review prompt (src/components/ReviewPrompt.tsx). Optional: when blank, the
"Rate Hearth" step shows only a thank-you with no button, since there is
nowhere to send anyone yet. Set once the app has a real App Store listing.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_STORE_URL=

# Set to 1 on Vercel Production once real payments start: makes an sk_test_ Stripe key fatal (src/lib/envGuard.ts).
# REQUIRE_LIVE_STRIPE=1
